From c2ec0a1a5b200eee2169926df6e54a08231760fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Season Tempo Build <claude@seasontempo.local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 18:56:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Migrations already applied to production

These four were applied to the production database before their files reached
the repository. Recorded here so migration history matches the schema that is
actually running.

  20260830014649  intake_apply persists the mailing address, and 'updated'
                  counts a real change instead of every row it touched
  20260830180256  intake_runs records column mapping and per-row decisions
  20260830181427  drop budget_items.actual, a stale second source of truth
  20260830183041  drop player_stats, an empty legacy statistics table

Nothing is reapplied. Applying migrations ahead of committing them was a
mistake: dropping the old intake_apply_run signature would have broken live
Import if PostgREST had not resolved the deployed five-argument call through
the new defaulted parameters.
